## Symfony 8.1 framework conventions

### Controllers

- Extend `Symfony\Bundle\FrameworkBundle\Controller\AbstractController`
- Service tag: `tags: ['controller.service_arguments']` in `config/services.yaml`
- Inject repositories/translators/services as action method arguments (autowired)
- Route attribute on class for prefix, on method for specific paths
- Return `Response` or render via `$this->render('template.html.twig', [...])`
- Redirect via `$this->redirectToRoute('route_name', ['_locale' => 'nl'])`

```php
#[Route(path: '/{_locale<%app.supported_locales%>}/dashboard/tracker')]
class DividendTrackerController extends AbstractController
{
    #[Route(path: '/dividend/{year}', name: 'dividend_tracker', requirements: ['year' => '\d+'])]
    public function index(
        PaymentRepository $paymentRepository,
        TranslatorInterface $translator,
        int $year = 1
    ): Response {
        return $this->render('dividend_tracker/index.html.twig', [...]);
    }
}
```

### Entities (Doctrine ORM)

- Use `Doctrine\ORM\Mapping as ORM` import, then `#[ORM\Table]`, `#[ORM\Column]`, etc.
- API Platform: `#[ApiResource(...)]` for REST exposure
- Serialization groups: `#[Groups(['group:read', 'group:write'])]`
- Fluent setters: return `: self` or `: static`
- Always `#[ORM\HasLifecycleCallbacks]` when using prePersist/postPersist etc.
- Use typed Collection: `Doctrine\Common\Collections\Collection` + `ArrayCollection`
- Specify `targetEntity:` in relation attributes when the target is a string name
- Always specify `inversedBy` / `mappedBy` on bidirectional relations

```php
#[ApiResource(
    normalizationContext: ['groups' => ['pie:read']],
    denormalizationContext: ['groups' => ['pie:write']],
    security: 'is_granted("ROLE_USER")',
    operations: [new Get(), new GetCollection(), new Post()]
)]
#[ORM\Table(name: 'pie')]
#[ORM\Entity(repositoryClass: 'App\Repository\PieRepository')]
class Pie
{
    #[ORM\Id]
    #[ORM\GeneratedValue(strategy: 'SEQUENCE')]
    #[ORM\Column(type: 'integer')]
    private ?int $id = null;

    #[Groups(['pie:read', 'pie:write'])]
    #[ORM\Column(type: 'string', length: 255)]
    private string $label;
}
```

### Forms

- Extend `Symfony\Component\Form\AbstractType`
- Implement `buildForm(FormBuilderInterface $builder, array $options): void`
- Implement `configureOptions(OptionsResolver $resolver): void`
- Use builder chaining: `$builder->add('field')->add('field2', null, ['required' => false])`
- Options resolver for defaults: `$resolver->setDefaults(['data_class' => Entity::class])`

### Services & DI

- Config in `config/services.yaml` with `autowire: true` (default)
- Fully-qualified class name as service ID: e.g. `App\Helper\DateHelper`
- Controller action arguments are autowired — no manual DI in controllers
- Event listeners: tag with `kernel.event_listener`, event name in `event:` and `method:`

### Security

- API Platform: `security: 'is_granted("ROLE_USER")'` in `#[ApiResource]`
- Route security goes in `config/packages/security.yaml` (if present)

### Twig templates

- Template path format: `controller_action.html.twig` in subdirectory per controller
- Translation: `$translator->trans('key')` in PHP, `{{ 'key'|trans }}` in Twig
- importmap for JS assets: use `{{ importmap('app') }}` in templates

### API Platform

- Operations: `new Get()`, `new GetCollection()`, `new Post()`, `new Put()`, `new Patch()`, `new Delete()`
- Normalization/denormalization context via groups
- Groups format: `entity:action` — e.g. `pie:read`, `transaction:write`

---

## Migration patterns (6.4 → 8.1)

These patterns fix code still on 6.4 conventions:

| 6.4 (oud) | 8.1 (nieuw) |
|---|---|
| `@Route(...)` annotation | `#[Route(...)]` attribute |
| `@ORM\Table(...)` annotation | `#[ORM\Table(...)]` attribute |
| `@Groups({...})` | `#[Groups([...])]` |
| `/** @var Type */` doc for props | `private Type $prop;` typed property |
| `function foo(): ReturnType` return after params | same — no change, but check colon spacing |
| `$this->container->get(id)` | constructor/argument injection |
| `@param`/`@return` for types | native type syntax; PHPDoc only for descriptions |
| `DateTime('Y-m-d')` | `new DateTime('Y-m-d')` |

Rector is configured in `rector.php` with sets:
- `DoctrineSetList::ANNOTATIONS_TO_ATTRIBUTES`
- `SymfonySetList::ANNOTATIONS_TO_ATTRIBUTES`
- `SensiolabsSetList::FRAMEWORK_EXTRA_61`

Run: `vendor/bin/rector process` (works on `src/`).

PHPStan analysis: `composer phpstan` (level 5, memory 1024M).  
CS check: `composer cscheck` (phpcs).  
CS fix: `composer csfix` (phpcbf).  
Tests: `composer phpunit` (with coverage).

---

## Architecture & design principles

### SOLID

- **Single Responsibility**: each class has one reason to change. Controllers handle routing+rendering only, Forms handle form building only, Entities are data+behavior only.
- **Open/Closed**: extend via dependency injection and interface implementation, not class modification.
- **Liskov**: interfaces (`Contracts/`) define contracts; implementations are swappable.
- **Interface Segregation**: small focused interfaces (`StockPricePluginInterface`, `DividendDatePluginInterface`).
- **Dependency Inversion**: high-level code depends on interfaces (in `Contracts/`), not concrete classes.

### DRY

- Extract repeated query logic into Repository methods
- Shared validation in Form types with `configureOptions()`
- Common view partials in `templates/_shared/` or via Twig `include`/`embed`

### KISS

- Controllers: thin — delegate business logic to services/repositories
- Forms: one class per form, no inheritance chains deeper than AbstractType → YourType
- Entities: plain objects with getters, fluent setters, and collection management

### Clean Architecture layers

```
src/
  Controller/       ← Framework layer (routing, HTTP)
  Form/             ← Input validation & construction
  Entity/           ← Domain models (Doctrine ORM)
  Repository/       ← Data access
  Contracts/        ← Interfaces / ports
    Service/        ←   Domain service interfaces
  Helper/           ← Pure utility functions (no DI)
  Serializer/       ← API Platform context builders
  State/            ← Post-processors
  Autocompleter/    ← UX autocomplete providers
  EventListener/    ← Kernel event listeners
  Doctrine/         ← Custom Doctrine types/functions
```

Dependencies point INWARD: Controller → Form/Service(interface) → Entity.  
No Entity depends on Controller. No Form depends on Repository directly.

### Language

- **Documentation**: English — all code comments, README, CONTRIBUTING, and project documentation must be in English
- **Git commits**: English — commit messages, PR titles, and CHANGELOG in English. Use conventional commits: `type(scope): description`
- **User-facing translations**: Dutch — via Symfony Translation system (`translations/*.yaml`), keys in PHP/Twig remain English

## Coding conventions

- **Attributes** before properties, properties before constructor, constructor before methods
- **Methods**: private helpers below public API
- **Fluent API**: setters return `: self` or `: static` for chaining
- **No magic numbers/strings**: define as `public const CONST_NAME = value` on the relevant class
- **Collections**: initialize in `__construct()` with `new ArrayCollection()`
- **Imports order**: 1) built-in (`DateTime`), 2) first-party (`App\*`), 3) Symfony, 4) Doctrine, 5) vendor
- **No `@var` type hints** in PHPDoc — use typed properties instead
- **No `@Annotation` syntax** — must use `#[Attribute]` syntax
- **Nullable entities**: `?` prefix, not `@param Type|null` in PHPDoc

---

## Upgrade pitfall checklist

- [ ] All `@Annotation` → `#[Attribute(...)]` converted (check with Rector, then verify edge cases)
- [ ] All `/** @var Type */` → typed property syntax
- [ ] All `@param`/`@return` type hints → native type syntax (PHPDoc only for descriptions)
- [ ] Service DI: `$this->container->get()` → constructor/method injection
- [ ] Route names match: `name: 'route_name'` in `#[Route]`, no stringly-typed names
- [ ] `#[ORM\GeneratedValue(strategy: 'SEQUENCE')]` not `'AUTO'` (Symfony standard)
- [ ] Entity relations use `targetEntity:` not class literal when referencing by string name
- [ ] Form `buildForm` → `configureOptions` split from legacy `setDefaultOptions`
- [ ] Remove any `use Symfony\Component\Something\Annotation\*` leftover imports
- [ ] Verify `config/services.yaml` autowiring covers all new service classes
- [ ] Run `composer phpstan` after each batch of changes — level 5 is strict
- [ ] Run `composer cscheck` — project follows PSR coding standard
- [ ] Rector can do bulk conversions; always review diff for edge cases afterwards